    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.starter\n\n### Description\n\nMaybe there's an option that already handles this which I couldn't find yet. If so, please, direct me to the answer / solution.\r\n\r\nI use `mini.starter` and when I start vim the command line displays for a fraction of a second `(mini.starter) Query:`. It would be nice if there would be an option to disable this behavior altogether. \r\n\r\nThis is obviously just a glitch and nothing with very high priority.",
